worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_12.js"
  ceiling 1216
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver: issue #658 divided one oversized worker file by line count, so this shard has no subject of its own. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into src/web/wasm-worker. The +18 lines over the previous 1198 ceiling are pure catalog data, not logic: hive-mind#2158 dispatched Hello World issues in Scala and Kotlin that no catalog language could answer, so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained scala and kotlin in Rust and this mirror gained the matching WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus their two hello_world templates. Mirroring only hello_world follows the existing sparse-coverage precedent (count_to_three carries 6 of 12 languages) and keeps every consumer of WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES consistent; the remaining task templates degrade through the blueprint and oracle fallbacks. This data moves to src/web/wasm-worker with the rest of the write-program surface."
